# Git workflow: confirm before publish (demo)

Work on a task branch. Before Git writes, check repository, branch, status, and diff.
Prepare changes, checks, a short commit message, and PR text within the task scope.
Before push and PR creation, show the ready diff, check results, target repository, base/head, and PR text. Wait for publish confirmation.
If the user already explicitly allowed publishing **this** PR, do not ask again. A general "implement the feature" ask is not publish confirmation.
Merge, release, and rewriting published history need a separate basis in the request or project rules.
